# Load-bearing, not housekeeping. The Dockerfile does `COPY app/ /app/`, so
# anything sitting in app/ that is not excluded here ships in a production image.

# Stale caches from local dev. Harmless at import (Python 3 will not import a
# .pyc without its .py in __pycache__), but they bloat the image and their
# mtimes break the build-time compileall's timestamp match, causing every module
# to be re-parsed on every run.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Tests live outside app/ in this layout, so they are not copied by the COPY
# above — listed anyway so the exclusion survives someone moving them in.
# Both spellings: this image uses `test/`, but `tests/` is the more common
# convention and would otherwise ship silently if the directory were renamed.
test/
tests/
conftest.py
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Never, under any circumstance. This container is credential-free by design:
# it talks to the internal API with a run token from the environment and to
# object storage over presigned URLs, and holds no S3 credentials at all.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials*
secrets*

# Local scratch that has a habit of appearing next to the code.
*.parquet
*.joblib
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/
scratch/
tmp/

# VCS and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# The Dockerfile itself and its siblings — outside app/, so not copied, but
# excluding them also keeps them out of the build context hash.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore